{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MobiusEnergy","lean:module:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.Basic"],"declarations":64,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_differs_forces_sep_differ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_differs_forces_sep_differ","kind":"theorem","line":1409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1409-L1423","doc":"**THE CHARGE-SIDE LOCALISATION.** Two instantiations whose `b₃` differ must\ndiffer in their pair or triple separations.\n\nRead with §9g: the many-body content and the charge-antisymmetric content of\nthis channel are the same obligation — a derived geometry — not two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_congr_of_sep_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_congr_of_sep_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1387-L1407","doc":"**The channel's `b₃` depends only on the pair and triple separations.**\n\nNote `Lquad` is unconstrained: `BindingMap.b3` is built from `pair` and\n`triple` alone, so the four-component assembly does not enter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_ne_zero_forces_moved_sep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_ne_zero_forces_moved_sep","kind":"theorem","line":1329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1329-L1343","doc":"**THE LOCALISATION.** A nonzero 3-body cumulant from this channel forces the\nassemblies to have moved the pair's separations.\n\nSo route (2)'s entire many-body content is the configuration change — read\nwith §9d, which rules out a topological floor, every number the channel can\nsupply is a derived geometry. AME2020's `b₃ = +1.4262225` MeV is nonzero, so\nthe hypothesis is not idle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_eq_zero_of_sep_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobius_b3_eq_zero_of_sep_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1318-L1327","doc":"**Hence the channel's 3-body cumulant vanishes identically** when the\nassemblies leave the separations alone. Composing the above with the\ncorpus's `b3_eq_zero_of_pairLocal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobiusCrossingModel_pairLocal_of_sep_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobiusCrossingModel_pairLocal_of_sep_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1309-L1316","doc":"**If the assemblies do not move the pair, the channel is pair-local.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobiusCrossingModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobiusCrossingModel","kind":"def","line":1299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1299-L1307","doc":"The crossing model the Möbius mutual channel induces, given one link\nembedding per assembly: the isolated pair, the triple containing `k`, and\nthe full four-component assembly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.innerPairEnergy_congr_of_sep_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.innerPairEnergy_congr_of_sep_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1286-L1297","doc":"**The pair energy depends on the pair's separations and nothing else.**\n\nThe per-`(i, j, s)` form of `mutualIntegrand_depends_only_on_sep`, which is\nwhat the pair-locality comparison actually needs: two *different* links\nagreeing on one pair's separations agree on that pair's energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_smul","kind":"theorem","line":1226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1226-L1239","doc":"**Scaling the separation by `c` scales the pair energy by `c⁻²`.**\n\nThe half `QOU.MobiusEnergy.mutualIntegrand_smul` says it cannot supply,\nnow that §3 has built the integral. Read it with the docstring above: the\nintegration interval does **not** scale, so this is the law for\nseparation-at-fixed-length, not for a similarity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mutualIntegrand_depends_only_on_sep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mutualIntegrand_depends_only_on_sep","kind":"theorem","line":1157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1157-L1170","doc":"**The `pointKnot` components of `separatedLink` do not weaken §9d** — a\nnote a reader is entitled to demand, proved rather than asserted.\n\n`separatedLink` populates both components with `pointKnot`, a degenerate\nembedding. That is irrelevant to the conclusion because `mutualIntegrand`,\nand hence `innerPairEnergy`, reads **only** the `sep` field — this states\nexactly that, so the component data provably cannot enter. It is the same\ndivision of labour §2's `shrinkingLink` uses, where the content is in `sep`\nand the components merely populate the structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.four_pi_is_the_largest_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.four_pi_is_the_largest_constant","kind":"theorem","line":1133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1133-L1155","doc":"**`4π` is the LARGEST constant that works** — the bound is sharp.\n\nThe first draft of this stated equality on the witness above and left the\nsharpness claim to the docstring. That is the defect this whole subsection\nexists to catch, one level up: a narrated inference is not a proved one. So\nthe claim is stated instead — any `c` for which `c·|lk| ≤ I energy` holds\nacross all satisfying data satisfies `c ≤ 4π`, because the witness has\n`lk = 1` and `I energy = 4π`.\n\nTogether with `four_pi_abs_lk_le_energy` this pins the constant exactly:\n`4π` works and nothing larger does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.four_pi_bound_hypotheses_satisfiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.four_pi_bound_hypotheses_satisfiable","kind":"theorem","line":1117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1117-L1131","doc":"**The hypotheses are satisfiable with a nonzero linking number.**\n\nA one-point parameter domain with `I = evaluation` is monotone and odd, and\nthe constant integrands `gauss = energy = 4π` satisfy the domination. The\nresulting `lk` is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.no_positive_uniform_mutual_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.no_positive_uniform_mutual_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":1088,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1088-L1102","doc":"**No positive constant lower-bounds the mutual pair energy.**\n\nSo the Möbius mutual channel carries no universal positive floor, and in\nparticular no topological invariant can bound it below by a positive\namount on a pairwise-unlinked pair. Route (2)'s magnitude has to come from\na *derived configuration* — a geometry — and not from the pair's link type.\n\nThis is a scope-(b) structural exclusion in the sense of AGENTS.md: the\ninvariant cited is `LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_le`, the separation bound\n§1 proves, and the exclusion is of *topological* lower bounds only. It says\nnothing against a geometric magnitude, which is what the framework would\nhave to derive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.uniformLowerBound_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.uniformLowerBound_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":1077,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1077-L1086","doc":"**No positive constant lower-bounds a quantity that gets arbitrarily\nsmall.** The abstract step; `no_positive_uniform_mutual_lower_bound`\ninstantiates it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.innerPairEnergy_separatedLink_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.innerPairEnergy_separatedLink_small","kind":"theorem","line":1065,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1065-L1075","doc":"**Every sufficiently small positive value is realised.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.innerPairEnergy_separatedLink_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.innerPairEnergy_separatedLink_le","kind":"theorem","line":1050,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1050-L1063","doc":"The pair energy of `separatedLink` is at most `1 / (1 + |R|)²` — §3's own\n`innerPairEnergy_le`, with the constant integrand discharging its\nmeasurability hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.separatedLink_hasUniformSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.separatedLink_hasUniformSeparation","kind":"theorem","line":1043,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1043-L1048","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.separatedLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.separatedLink","kind":"def","line":1022,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1022-L1041","doc":"A two-component link whose components sit at **constant** separation\n`1 + |R|`. The `1 +` keeps it positive for every real `R`, so the family is\nindexed by all of `ℝ` with no side condition to carry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.lk_bound_iff_nonneg_of_lk_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.lk_bound_iff_nonneg_of_lk_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1008,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L1008-L1020","doc":"**At `lk = 0` the link bound IS non-negativity.**\n\nStated as an `iff` so that \"the bound adds nothing\" is proved rather than\nasserted: its conclusion is *equivalent* to `0 ≤ E_mutual`, which §3's\n`LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_nonneg` already supplies with no hypotheses.\n\nEvery pairwise linking number of the Borromean link vanishes, so this is the\ncase `qou-o6ml` route (2) actually faces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.four_pi_abs_lk_le_energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.four_pi_abs_lk_le_energy","kind":"theorem","line":974,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L974-L1004","doc":"**`4π |lk| ≤ E_mutual`** — the link analogue of BFHW's Theorem D.\n\nHypotheses, all visible and none of them the conclusion:\n\n* `hmono` / `hneg` — the integral is monotone and odd. Standard properties\n  of the Lebesgue integral; abstracted so this statement does not depend on\n  which integral is used.\n* `hgauss` — **Gauss's integral formula** `∫ gauss = 4π·lk`. Classical, and\n  the one genuinely assumed input.\n* `hdom` — the pointwise domination, **proved** in §9b for the ℝ³\n  integrands.\n\nThe derivation is `|∫ g| ≤ ∫ |g| ≤ ∫ e`; the content is that `hdom` is\navailable at all, and that is §9b's determinant estimate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.gaussIntegrand_le_mutualIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.gaussIntegrand_le_mutualIntegrand","kind":"theorem","line":951,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L951-L970","doc":"**The pointwise domination.**\n\n`|det(a,b,c)| / ‖c‖³ ≤ ‖a‖‖b‖ / ‖c‖²`. This is the whole geometric content\nof the link bound: one power of `‖c‖` from the determinant estimate cancels\nagainst the cube in the Gauss kernel, leaving precisely the inverse-square\nMöbius kernel that §7 and §8 force by symmetry.\n\nIt is **proved**, not assumed — `four_pi_abs_lk_le_energy` below takes the\ndomination as a hypothesis because it is stated over an abstract parameter\ndomain, and this is what discharges it in the concrete ℝ³ case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.abs_det3_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.abs_det3_le","kind":"theorem","line":937,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L937-L947","doc":"**`|det3| ≤ ‖a‖ ‖b‖ ‖c‖`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.det3_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.det3_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":916,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L916-L935","doc":"**`det3² ≤ ‖a‖²‖b‖²‖c‖²`** — Cauchy–Schwarz against `a × b`, then Lagrange\nto drop the `⟪a,b⟫²` that only helps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.cauchySchwarz3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.cauchySchwarz3","kind":"theorem","line":909,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L909-L914","doc":"**Cauchy–Schwarz in ℝ³**, in coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.lagrange3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.lagrange3","kind":"theorem","line":901,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L901-L907","doc":"**Lagrange's identity in ℝ³** — `‖a × b‖² = ‖a‖²‖b‖² − ⟪a,b⟫²`. A `ring`\nidentity; it is what makes the cross-product bound free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.nrm3_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.nrm3_sq","kind":"theorem","line":897,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L897-L899","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.nrm3_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.nrm3_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":895,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L895-L895","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.nrm3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.nrm3","kind":"def","line":892,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L892-L893","doc":"The Euclidean norm on ℝ³, in coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.det3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.det3","kind":"def","line":888,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L888-L890","doc":"The scalar triple product `(a × b) · c`, in coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.flat_measure_not_mobiusInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.flat_measure_not_mobiusInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":790,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L790-L806","doc":"**§7c — the FLAT parameter measure is not Möbius invariant.**\n\nDropping the arclength Jacobians leaves the bare kernel, and it does *not*\nsurvive an inversion. Witness: chord `1`, centre distances `2` and `1`, so\nthe transformed chord is `1/2` and the kernel reads `4` against the original\n`1`.\n\nThis is the exact assumption §6 removed rather than documented, now shown to\nbe not merely unsupported but **false**: `ds dt` cannot be the measure the\nMöbius channel is carried against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.inverse_square_mobiusInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.inverse_square_mobiusInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":779,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L779-L788","doc":"The converse: the inverse-square kernel really is Möbius invariant, so the\ncharacterisation above is not vacuous. Together with it, `1/d²` is the\nunique Möbius-invariant separation kernel up to scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobiusInvariant_forces_inverse_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.mobiusInvariant_forces_inverse_square","kind":"theorem","line":731,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L731-L777","doc":"**THE DISCRIMINATOR.** Möbius invariance forces the inverse square.\n\nNo ansatz, no fitted exponent, no appeal to the measured numbers: the\nhypothesis is the symmetry alone, and the conclusion is the kernel. Any\norientation-blind functional of separation that is Möbius invariant against\nthe arclength density *is* `f(1)/d²` — so the mutual channel's `1 / sep ^ 2`\nis the unique such kernel up to the overall constant.\n\nThis is what §§1-6 could not supply. Those sections admit a whole class of\ncandidates; this one cuts the class to a single ray.\n\n**🛑 SCOPE — the hypothesis is stronger than the geometry supplies, and the\ngap is at small chord.** `MobiusInvariantKernel` quantifies over\n*unconstrained* positive triples `(d, da, db)`. A geometrically realisable\ntriple is three distances among three points of `ℝ³`, so it must satisfy the\ntriangle inequalities; the witness this proof uses, `(1, 1/d, 1)`, needs\n`1/d ≤ 2`, i.e. **`d ≥ 1/2`**. For `d < 1/2` that triple is not realisable by\nany configuration, so the conclusion at small `d` rests on invariance over\ntriples the geometry never presents.\n\nTaking `da = db = 1/√d` instead is realisable for `d ≤ 4` and fails past it,\nso neither single *witness family* covers `(0, ∞)`.\n\n**🟩 RESOLVED in §8 below — this caveat is retained as the record of the gap,\nnot as a live one.** The restricted hypothesis gives the same conclusion:\n`realisable_forces_inverse_square` proves `f x = f 1 / x ^ 2` on all of\n`(0, ∞)` from `MobiusInvariantOnRealisable` alone. The gap was in the search,\nnot in the mathematics — looking for ONE witness family missed that the\nrealisable hypothesis is a two-parameter family, and the isosceles\nconfiguration `da = db = t` bootstraps from `(0, 4]` to everything.\n\nSo this theorem MAY now be cited as forced by invariance over geometrically\nrealisable triples; cite `realisable_forces_inverse_square` when that is the\nhypothesis you have. Bean `qou-zfs6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.MobiusInvariantKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.MobiusInvariantKernel","kind":"def","line":721,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L721-L729","doc":"**Möbius invariance of a separation kernel, carried against arclength.**\n\n`f` is the kernel as a function of separation; `d` is the chord between the\ntwo points; `da`, `db` are their distances to the inversion centre. The\nleft-hand side is the transformed integrand: the kernel evaluated at the\ntransformed chord, times the two arclength Jacobians. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.weightedPairMean_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.weightedPairMean_one","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L665-L670","doc":"**`w = 1` recovers §5 exactly**, so the flat-measure statement is the\nconstant-density instance of the general one rather than a separate claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernelW_integral_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernelW_integral_zero","kind":"theorem","line":641,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L641-L663","doc":"**O2 against an arbitrary density.** The subtracted kernel has zero mean\nwith respect to `w`, whatever `w` is — so the clearance no longer depends on\nwhich measure the fibre supplies, and in particular holds for arclength.\n\nThe subtraction constant is still forced rather than chosen: it is the\nkernel's own `w`-mean, exactly as `c₀ = ⟨coth⟩_M` was forced in #7080. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernelW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernelW","kind":"def","line":636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L636-L639","doc":"The mutual kernel with its own `w`-weighted mean subtracted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.weightedPairMean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.weightedPairMean","kind":"def","line":629,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L629-L634","doc":"The **`w`-weighted mean** of the mutual integrand over the second\ncomponent's parameter. With `w = |γ'|` this is the arclength mean the\nO'Hara energy actually uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernel_not_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernel_not_pos","kind":"theorem","line":584,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L584-L604","doc":"**And it genuinely changes sign** — it is not everywhere positive.\n\nThis is what makes the O2 clearance real rather than formal: a kernel whose\nmean is zero cannot be strictly positive throughout, so the subtraction has\nactually moved the channel out of the class `coth` was excluded from. The\ncontrast with `mutualIntegrand_pos_of_ne`, which holds with no hypothesis\nwhatsoever, is the whole content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernel_integral_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernel_integral_zero","kind":"theorem","line":571,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L571-L582","doc":"**The subtracted kernel satisfies O2.** Its mean over the parameter\ninterval is exactly zero — which is the condition `∫_M Δu = 0` imposes and\nthe unsubtracted kernel provably cannot meet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.zeroMeanMutualKernel","kind":"def","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L564-L569","doc":"The **zero-mean mutual kernel**: the mutual integrand with its own mean\nsubtracted. The subtraction constant is `innerPairEnergy`, i.e. the mean\nitself — determined by the link, never chosen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_ge","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L501-L525","doc":"**The pair energy is bounded away from zero.**\n\nWith `innerPairEnergy_le` this brackets the per-pair contribution into\n`[1/D², 1/δ²]`, both endpoints positive and both built from distances\nalone. A functional pinned inside a strictly positive interval cannot\ncancel, whatever the link's orientation data does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.HasBoundedSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.HasBoundedSeparation","kind":"def","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L495-L499","doc":"A link is **confined to diameter `D`** when no two points on distinct\ncomponents are more than `D` apart — automatic for a link in a bounded\nregion, and carried explicitly for the same reason the lower gap is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L473-L486","doc":"**The pair energy is blind to orientation reversal.**\n\nA genuine change of variables `u = 1 - t` across the unit parameter\ninterval, which the substitution preserves. This is the gate: the exchange\nthat sends `μ̄₁₂₃ ↦ −μ̄₁₂₃` leaves this functional's value untouched, so it\nis even in `μ̄₁₂₃` — indeed independent of it — and is not the odd\nfunctional `odd_symmetric_functional_vanishes` annihilates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L468-L471","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.reverse_sep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.reverse_sep","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L465-L466","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.reverse","kind":"def","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L455-L463","doc":"Reverse every component of a link simultaneously — the operation under\nwhich an oriented invariant such as `μ̄₁₂₃` changes sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.reverse","kind":"def","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L436-L447","doc":"Reverse a component's parametrisation, `s ↦ 1 - s`. Every distance field is\nprecomposed; every law carries over because the substitution is an\ninvolution of the parameter interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_le","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L382-L400","doc":"**The inner pair energy carries the bound through the integral.**\n\nOver a unit parameter interval the integral of something `≤ 1/δ²` is itself\n`≤ 1/δ²`. Together with `innerPairEnergy_nonneg` this pins the per-pair\ncontribution into `[0, 1/δ²]` — a finite value derived from the link's\ngeometry, with no fitted constant anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L374-L380","doc":"**The inner pair energy is non-negative**, inherited from the integrand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.innerPairEnergy","kind":"def","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L368-L372","doc":"The **inner pair energy** at fixed `s`: an honest `intervalIntegral` of the\nmutual integrand over the second component's parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_intervalIntegrable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_intervalIntegrable","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L349-L366","doc":"**The mutual integrand is interval-integrable.**\n\nBounded (by `mutualIntegrand_le_of_uniformSeparation`) and measurable on a\nfinite interval. This is the statement `QOU.MobiusEnergy` says it cannot\nmake — and it costs no analysis beyond the uniform gap, because the mutual\nchannel has no diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.realisable_forces_inverse_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.realisable_forces_inverse_square","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L309-L334","doc":"**§7's open sub-item, closed: the restricted hypothesis still forces the\ninverse square, on all of `(0, ∞)`.**\n\nSo `mobiusInvariant_forces_inverse_square` may be cited without its\nrealisability caveat: no conclusion of §7 depended on triples the geometry\ncannot present. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.realisable_inverse_square_of_le_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.realisable_inverse_square_of_le_four","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L283-L307","doc":"Step one: the characterisation on `(0, 4]`, from `c = 1` and `t = 1/√x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.isoscelesStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.isoscelesStep","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L268-L281","doc":"**The isosceles step.** With the inversion centre equidistant from both\ncurve points (`da = db = t`), only `c ≤ 2t` binds, and invariance becomes a\nclean scaling law. This is the two-parameter freedom §7's single-witness\nsearch missed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.MobiusInvariantOnRealisable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.MobiusInvariantOnRealisable","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L261-L266","doc":"**Möbius invariance restricted to realisable triples** — the honest\nhypothesis §7 wished it had. Strictly weaker than `MobiusInvariantKernel`,\nwhich quantifies over all positive triples. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.Realisable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.Realisable","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L254-L259","doc":"**Geometric realisability of a distance triple.** `(d, da, db)` are the\npairwise distances of three points of `ℝ³` — the chord `d` between the two\ncurve points, and their distances `da`, `db` to the inversion centre — iff\nthey are positive and satisfy the three triangle inequalities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.disjoint_not_imp_uniformSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.disjoint_not_imp_uniformSeparation","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L184-L213","doc":"**`disjoint` does not imply `HasUniformSeparation`.**\n\nThe `shrinkingLink` satisfies every `LinkEmbedding` field — in particular\n`disjoint`, so its mutual integrand is positive everywhere — and admits no\nuniform gap whatsoever.\n\nConsequence: the bound in `mutualIntegrand_le_of_uniformSeparation` is a\ngenuine additional hypothesis about the link, not repackaged `disjoint`.\nConcretely, this is where compactness of the components enters the mutual\nchannel; drop it and the integrals below cease to exist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.shrinkingLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.shrinkingLink","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L163-L182","doc":"The counterexample link: two components, disjoint everywhere, separation\ndecaying to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.decayingSep_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.decayingSep_symm","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L160-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.decayingSep_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.decayingSep_pos","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L155-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.decayingSep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.decayingSep","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L151-L153","doc":"Separation that is **positive everywhere and has infimum zero**: it decays\nas either parameter runs off to infinity. Symmetric by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.pointKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusMutualChannel.pointKnot","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L138-L149","doc":"A degenerate knot embedding: one point, all distances zero. Used only to\npopulate the components of the counterexample link, whose content is in its\n`sep` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_nonneg_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_nonneg_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L115-L119","doc":"The mutual integrand is non-negative on distinct components — the lower\nhalf of the bound, recorded so `‖·‖` can be discharged below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_le_of_uniformSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_le_of_uniformSeparation","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L100-L113","doc":"**The mutual integrand is bounded on distinct components.**\n\nThis is the whole prune: `1/sep²` is bounded because `sep` is bounded\n*below*, and `sep` is bounded below because the components are disjoint.\nNo diagonal, no singularity, no O'Hara theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.HasUniformSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.HasUniformSeparation","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusMutualChannel.lean#L89-L98","doc":"A link has **uniform separation `δ`** when distinct components stay at least\n`δ` apart, uniformly in both parameters.\n\nFor a genuine link — finitely many disjoint *compact* components — this is\nthe distance between disjoint compacts and is automatic. It is carried here\nas an explicit hypothesis because `LinkEmbedding.disjoint` supplies only\n*pointwise* positivity, and `disjoint_not_imp_uniformSeparation` below\nproves that the two are genuinely different. ","signatureChunk":0}]}